I think that sort of thing is a necessary consequence of the way the game
strives both to be challenging and random; sometimes exceptionally tough
or easy situations will be thrown up. That doesn't mean that some of the
extreme cases - which this one is not, really - can't be eliminated
without giving rise to the Angband problem where monster and item depths
are so closely restricted that the randomness is almost a matter of mere
layout.
